e period growing up because  she was a tomboy and so her parents  didn't think anything about maybe her  sexuality is leaning a certain way  because it's okay for her to be a tomboy  as long as she doesn't stay that way and  eventually grows out of it and look at  that she never did  here's another thing one though the ones  that aren't notably young teens early  20s they're unmarried they're unattached  so some of the prime examples Vasquez  from aliens and yes facias is a  problematic character because the  actresses in brown face but let's that's  not the topic for this video but Vasquez  not excessively young but in the  military with no hint of an interest  sexually in any of the men around her  Brienne of Tarth who while she has her  crush on Jaime and holy crap did they  screw that up by the end she has seems  to have accepted in her life at least in  the TV show I've read the books I'm a  I'm a fake geek person but she seems to  have accepted that she is not going to  have romantic entanglements that was the  price of getting to do these other  things that she wanted to do  I mentioned the league of their own now  first of all a league of their own  actually one of my favorite movies ever  and that's big for me because I hate  sports movies but I love alia there I'll  love it to death  now kit is the tomboy character and  she's very much focused on the game on  you know the progress on getting better  her sister played by Gina Davis Dottie  she is much more feminine much less  boyish and she's married again feeding  into this notion that to be a tomboy is  not just to embrace mass traditionally  masculine things but is to miss out on  feminine things  it's actually one of the plot points  going on with the character in the  original bad news bears she worries that  her interest in sports and guy things  means that guys won't ever want to date  her because they'll see her as one of  the guys and this does on an  undercurrent get reinforced by the fact  that t